  "behavior": [
    "A synchronous preorder visit includes its root. Zero stops normally, nonzero continues, and checked callback errors reach the original caller.",
    "The root keeps its native reference throughout traversal. Changing the child lists currently covered by the traversal returns Busy, including after nested traversal returns. Independent scene edits remain available.",
    "Traversal checks the same 32-level limit as other native shape operations.",
    "The callback record expires after the callback. Reading a shape or scene yields a nullable independently retained view, including when the receiver is closed during the callback.",
    "The measured workload visits the same graph 1000 times using a warmed visitor that only reads the kind. It records zero XRT allocations for language and direct C across all four link modes. The separate injected failure path records balanced allocation and release."
  ],
